{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/497743-corruptions","id":497743,"title":"Corruptions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-30T12:45:10-07:00","id":497743,"title":"Corruptions","content":"Something that I just thought of in another thread: what if, instead of a single Centimani non-Refinement, we had a set of Corruptions existing in parallel with the Refinements? Conceptually, each Corruption would take the principles of one of the Refinements and would twist it away from the Pilgrimage, shifting its goals to something other than the pursuit of Mortality. Mechanically, each Corruption would have two sets of Transmutations associated with it: the Pandoran Transmutations, and one of the two sets of Transmutations that the Refinement that it distorts is based on. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T13:24:18-07:00","id":497803,"title":"","content":"I like the idea, certainly - it would be interesting to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T14:16:19-07:00","id":497875,"title":"","content":"Nice plan.<br /> <br /> Centimani versions of refinements could be them embracing them at their worst; Cuprum becomes misanthropic and territorial, Stannum creates wrongs against itself to punish, Ferrum becomes a bully...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T14:29:39-07:00","id":497885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/497743-corruptions?p=497875#post497875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice plan.<br /> <br /> Centimani versions of refinements could be them embracing them at their worst; Cuprum becomes misanthropic and territorial, Stannum creates wrongs against itself to punish, Ferrum becomes a bully...</div> </div> </div> </div>What does Aurum become? Trying to mimic humanity's worst qualities? Or an utter rejection of humanity entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T05:46:56-07:00","id":498738,"title":"","content":"I think this falls into the trap of thinking of Centimani as representing evil, hence the &quot;evil versions&quot; of the Refinements being suggested. One of the things that 2nd edition seeks to stress is that humanity includes the good and the bad. Compassion, love, and hope are part of the human experience, but so is bigotry, selfishness, and despair. The Refinements explore humanity as a whole, not just the nice parts. What Centimani have done is rejected the path to Humanity, for whatever reason. They aren't necessarily evil. Some have just lost themselves to despair. I even wrote one example who gives up the Pilgrimage for a noble purpose, sacrificing himself for his throng-mates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T06:32:17-07:00","id":498759,"title":"","content":"FWIW, \u201cCorruptions are evil!&quot; was not part of my original pitch; merely veering away from the Pilgrimage in ways that otherwise echo the Refinements. For instance, at least one of them might be transhumanist in nature, seeking to surpass humanity's limitations instead of accepting them. And the guy who abandons the Pilgrimage for the sake of his throng-mates? Corrupted Aes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:21:38-07:00","id":498809,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver, something along those lines?<br /> <br /> Corrupted Aurum - Controlling humanity rather than being a part of it<br /> Corrupted Ferrum - Perfecting your body above human means (extra arms help in a wrestle, don't they?)<br /> Corrupted Mercurius - Study of Flux rather than Pyros as a whole<br /> Corrupted Argentum - Seeking to become the things you study (Vampire, Werewolves, Mage, whatev)<br /> Corrupted Aes - Helpling humanity in inhuman ways<br /> Corrupted Plumbum - Seeking to perfect your current state rather than understanding it (Prometheanist rather than humanist or post-humanist or trans-humanist)<br /> Corrupted Stannum - Rage against humanity rather than against humans<br /> Corrupted Cuprum - Becoming more animal than human, excluding yourself from humanity entirely<br /> Corrupted Cobalus - Focus on creating imperfections rather than exploring or fixing them","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:32:19-07:00","id":498818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/497743-corruptions?p=498738#post498738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this falls into the trap of thinking of Centimani as representing evil, hence the &quot;evil versions&quot; of the Refinements being suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div>So from that perspective, Corrupted Aurum might be a rejection of human qualities - the periodically discussed idea of a superhuman/transhuman refinement - or maybe a desire to rule and control humans (expressed malevolently or paternalistically). Corrupted Cuprum might be a solipsistic path - though I'm not sure how to differentiate it from the first version of corrupted Aurum - so maybe use the second version of Aurum. Corrupted Ferrum might be an obsession with the body and moulding it into different forms, at the expense of all else. Corrupted Mercurius would be an obsession with the Fire and losing yourself to it - more or less the Centimani we already have - ah, yes it's that but bent towards Flux, while Corrupted Plumbum is the same thing but bent towards Azoth, which makes for an obsession with being a better Promethean. Corrupted Stannum does make sense as an evil one, hurting people for the sake of it. Dataweaver's already suggested a model for Corrupted Aes. Corrupted Argentum might still be an attempt to follow a Pilgrimmage, but to become a kind of supernatural. rather than a human. Corrupted Cobalus might be obsessed with converting as many humans as possible into Prometheans (think Doctor Who's Cybermen), seeing it as a better way to be.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T22:31:44-07:00","id":499830,"title":"","content":"I personally would love to see something in Promethean 2e that follows a path of studying Flux. I'd like to think of more of a balance between Flux and Pyros, like the balance in Werewolf 2e between Flesh and Spirit. I think having some chaos in a Promethean will benefit their Great Work, humans are not creatures of pure order and logic after all. We are equally chaotic and prone to emotion. Now whilst Prometheans have that emotional instability of Torment, something leaning towards finding an emotional balance using Flux is something I'd like to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:04:51-07:00","id":499876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/497743-corruptions?p=499830#post499830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally would love to see something in Promethean 2e that follows a path of studying Flux. I'd like to think of more of a balance between Flux and Pyros, like the balance in Werewolf 2e between Flesh and Spirit. I think having some chaos in a Promethean will benefit their Great Work, humans are not creatures of pure order and logic after all. We are equally chaotic and prone to emotion. Now whilst Prometheans have that emotional instability of Torment, something leaning towards finding an emotional balance using Flux is something I'd like to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the problem with this is that, much like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/297978-changling-2-0-fan-idea-clarity-breaking-points?p=301515#post301515\">making &quot;becoming too certain of reality&quot; a legitimate contrasting issue to losing your sanity as a result of strain on the Clarity of a mind broken by exposure to a fairyland of raw possibility</a>, the &quot;chaotic&quot; end is narratively and metaphysically weighted disproportionately to the &quot;orderly&quot; end by dint of simple entropy \u2014 the universe does not get <i>more</i> ordered as time goes on, save in the absolute least useful fashion of &quot;progressively more material reaches a state in which it cannot be put to use&quot;\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026which you'll recall is <i>what Flux is</i> \u2014 it's the name for the aspects of the Fire that lead to dissolution, calcification, and directionless mutation. There's a <i>reason</i> the contrasting aspect of the Pyros to Flux in conventional thought is the one that most directly resonates with <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telos\" target=\"_blank\"><i>telos</i></a>.<br /> <br /> Flux is not a lively and healthy chaos. It's the inescapable fact that, among other things\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/379384-centimani-based-chronicle?p=383368#post383368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Promethean is a half-formed creature animated with the volatile energy of transformation and decay. This energy is ultimately chaotic and will eventually tear them apart, eroding their mind and body, unless it is harnessed to transform them into something more stable.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-02-2015, 02:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:50:26-07:00","id":500342,"title":"","content":"Remember, you're running around on fire. You don't solve that by hugging more fires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:53:55-07:00","id":500460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/497743-corruptions?p=499876#post499876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the problem with this is that, much like <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/297978-changling-2-0-fan-idea-clarity-breaking-points?p=301515#post301515\">making &quot;becoming too certain of reality&quot; a legitimate contrasting issue to losing your sanity as a result of strain on the Clarity of a mind broken by exposure to a fairyland of raw possibility</a>, the &quot;chaotic&quot; end is narratively and metaphysically weighted disproportionately to the &quot;orderly&quot; end by dint of simple entropy \u2014 the universe does not get <i>more</i> ordered as time goes on, save in the absolute least useful fashion of &quot;progressively more material reaches a state in which it cannot be put to use&quot;\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026which you'll recall is <i>what Flux is</i> \u2014 it's the name for the aspects of the Fire that lead to dissolution, calcification, and directionless mutation. There's a <i>reason</i> the contrasting aspect of the Pyros to Flux in conventional thought is the one that most directly resonates with <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telos\" target=\"_blank\"><i>telos</i></a>.<br /> <br /> Flux is not a lively and healthy chaos. It's the inescapable fact that, among other things\u2026<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps, then, one might study Flux to arrive at an acceptance of the mortality that comes with Humanity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T09:00:46-07:00","id":500464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/497743-corruptions?p=500460#post500460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps, then, one might study Flux to arrive at an acceptance of the mortality that comes with Humanity?</div> </div> </div> </div>You literally <i>have to die</i> before you can become human in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T23:04:29-07:00","id":501398,"title":"","content":"I like the option being there which malonkey1 says, tbh. I can clearly see that everything thinks studying Flux is <i>Bad Wrong Fun</i>, but perhaps it can be something in regards to what Centimani was, but in knowing Flux, it also would work to help avoid it in the future. Kinda like a version of Cobalus, a path of refinement to do with knowing something that is bad to guard against it. YMMV clearly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T09:15:3